-- DialogueData (ModuleScript, ReplicatedStorage)
-- NPC definitions + branching dialogue trees.  Content is PLACEHOLDER WRITING - replace with your lore.
--
-- Node:   { Text = "...", Choices = { Choice, ... } }
-- Choice: { Text = "...", Next = "nodeId" }              -> go to another node
--         { Text = "...", Action = { Type = ..., ... } } -> do something on the SERVER, then close
-- Action types handled by NPCService:
--   { Type = "OpenShop", ShopId = "..." }
--   { Type = "OfferMission", MissionId = "..." }   (ASSUMPTION: ids must exist in your MissionData)
--   { Type = "CompleteMission", MissionId = "..." } (turn-in; server re-checks objectives are done)
--   { Type = "Heal" }
--   { Type = "Close" }
--
-- CONDITIONS (checked on the server every time a node is shown AND when a choice is picked):
--   Choice.Requires = { MissionNotStarted = id } | { MissionActive = id } | { MissionReady = id } | { MissionCompleted = id }
--     -> choice is hidden unless the condition is true
--   Node.Redirect = { { Requires = {...}, To = "otherNode" }, ... }
--     -> first matching redirect replaces this node (use on "greet" to give NPCs different openers)
--
-- NPC placement: NPCService looks for Parts tagged "NPCSpawn" with attribute NpcId = "<key below>".
-- If MapBuilder doesn't create those, NPCs fall back to a ring around the first SpawnLocation.

